**RR-13 — Independent statistical adequacy assessment for the ingested registry** — DONE (2026-04-29)
The current registry is traceable and internally gated, but that does not prove it is a
complete/honest translation of the source corpus. Build an independent statistical
assessment lane: stratified sample over document, authority class, modality, lifecycle
bucket, and high-risk source shapes; blind human review against source windows; explicit
error taxonomy for omission, over-promotion, under-promotion, wrong modality/authority,
bad quote support, bad split/bundle shape, and duplicate/redundant records; acceptance
thresholds with confidence intervals. This should assess both accepted records and source
windows with no accepted output so omissions are measurable.
Completed as a same-agent first-pass review (not a strict external audit) in
`quality/adequacy/adequacy_2026-04-29-rr13-80-20/`. Result: 35/48 sampled records were
clean; 6/48 had major bad quote support, 6/48 were source-supported under-promotions due
quote-shape defects, and 1/48 had overstated authority/modality metadata. Section review
found 3/12 material-omission windows with 19 estimated missing actionable requirements.
Conclusion before repair: the registry was traceable, but not yet fit as a complete
actionable translation. The sampled blockers were then fixed directly in RR-14 to RR-16.
Impact: H | Effort: M

